</title>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0A1626009001">
<title>
Radiator Cooling Fan Operation
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Connect SUZUKI scan tool to DLC (1) with ignition “OFF”.
</ptxt>
<servicetool>
<servicetoolitem id = "L1F202">
<s-part>
(A)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "NNNNN-00035">
SUZUKI scan tool (Suzuki SDT-II)
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
</servicetool>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0A161010.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "87.737mm" ver = "01" gw = "205" gh = "232"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Set ignition “ON” and clear DTC. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1124004"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Select “Radiator Fan” function in “Active Test”. 
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check radiator cooling fan operation at low, mid and high modes.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If any abnormality is found, check cooling fan control system. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1624002"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
